@startuml Anonymous Source Verification System — Submission Flow

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #444444
    ActorBorderColor #444444
    LifeLineBorderColor #888888
    ParticipantBorderColor #444444
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
    ParticipantFontColor #222222
    BoxBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
    BoxBorderColor #CCCCCC
}

actor       "Anonymous Source"  as Source
participant "Frontend\n(React/TS)"  as FE
participant "Ingestion\nService"    as Ingest
participant "Encrypted\nFile Store" as Store
participant "PostgreSQL\nMetadata DB" as DB
participant "Redis\n(Broker + Cache)" as Redis
participant "Celery\nWorker" as Worker
participant "Timestamping\nService"  as TS
participant "RFC 3161 TSA\n(FreeTSA.org)" as TSA
participant "OpenTimestamps\n(Bitcoin)"   as OTS
participant "Analysis\nEngine (LLM)"      as LLM
participant "Certificate\nService"        as Cert

== 1. Evidence Upload ==

Source -> FE : Select evidence files +\noptional metadata
FE -> Ingest : POST /api/submissions\n(multipart, files + metadata)

group Ingestion
    Ingest -> Ingest : SHA-256 each file
    Ingest -> Ingest : Build Merkle tree across all file hashes
    Ingest -> Ingest : Compute Merkle root
    Ingest -> Ingest : Compute per-file proof paths\n(sibling hash list from leaf to root)
    Ingest -> Ingest : Generate submission_id\n(UUIDv4, no PII)
    Ingest -> Store  : Encrypt & store files\n(AES-256-GCM, per-file key)
    Ingest -> DB     : INSERT submission record\n(id, merkle_root, proof_paths, status=INGESTED)
    Ingest -> Redis  : SET submission:{id}:status = INGESTED
    Ingest -> Redis  : Enqueue Celery task chain\n(timestamp → analyze → certify)
    Ingest --> FE    : 202 Accepted\n{ submission_id }
end

FE --> Source : Show submission_id\n& progress dashboard

== 2. Async Pipeline (Celery Worker) ==

Redis -> Worker : Dequeue pipeline task chain

== 3. Timestamping ==

Worker -> TS : Execute timestamp_submission task

group RFC 3161 Trusted Timestamp (Primary)
    TS -> TSA : Send merkle_root hash
    TSA --> TS : Signed .tsr token\n(hash + TSA signature + UTC timestamp)
    TS -> Store : Store .tsr token
    TS -> DB   : UPDATE submission\n(rfc3161_token_hash, rfc3161_timestamp)
end

group OpenTimestamps — Bitcoin Anchor (Secondary)
    TS -> OTS : Submit merkle_root hash
    OTS --> TS : .ots receipt\n(pending Bitcoin confirmation)
    TS -> Store : Store .ots file
    TS -> DB    : UPDATE submission\n(ots_file_hash, status=TIMESTAMPED)
    TS -> Redis : SET submission:{id}:status = TIMESTAMPED
    note over OTS : Bitcoin block confirmed\n(~10 min, OP_RETURN)\nCelery Beat polls every 5 min
    OTS --> Worker  : Block height & block timestamp
    Worker -> DB    : UPDATE submission\n(bitcoin_block, block_timestamp)
end

== 4. Evidence Analysis ==

Worker -> LLM : Execute analyze_submission task\n(anonymized file contents + metadata)

group LLM Analysis Engine
    LLM -> LLM : Evaluate Consistency\n(facts, dates, names agree?)
    LLM -> LLM : Evaluate Corroboration\n(independent sources / doc types)
    LLM -> LLM : Evaluate Plausibility\n(known formats & institutional practices)
    LLM -> LLM : Extract evidence types,\nkey claims, red flags
    LLM --> Worker : Structured JSON scores\n{ consistency, corroboration,\n  plausibility, overall, reliability_class }
    Worker -> DB    : UPDATE submission\n(analysis scores, status=ANALYZED)
    Worker -> Redis : SET submission:{id}:status = ANALYZED
end

== 5. Certificate Generation ==

Worker -> Cert : Execute generate_certificate task

group Certificate Service
    Cert -> DB   : Read submission +\nanalysis + timestamp proofs
    Cert -> Cert : Build VerificationCertificate\n(CERT-YYYY-XXXXXX)
    Cert -> Cert : Generate attribution\nlanguage snippets
    Cert -> DB   : INSERT certificate\n(no PII, no file contents)
    Cert --> Worker : certificate_id
    Worker -> DB    : UPDATE submission\n(status=COMPLETE)
    Worker -> Redis : SET submission:{id}:status = COMPLETE
end

== 6. Certificate Retrieval ==

Source -> FE  : Poll status
FE -> Redis   : GET /api/submissions/{id}/status\n(reads Redis key — no DB hit)
Redis --> FE  : { status: COMPLETE }

FE -> Cert    : GET /api/submissions/{id}/certificate
Cert -> DB    : Fetch certificate
DB --> Cert   : VerificationCertificate JSON
Cert --> FE   : Certificate JSON\n(scores, timestamp proofs,\nper-file merkle_proof paths,\nattribution language)

FE --> Source : Display Certificate Viewer\n(confidence scores, proofs,\ncopy-ready attribution text)

== 7. Selective Disclosure (Optional) ==

note over Source, Cert
  A journalist can authenticate a single file without
  revealing other files in the bundle:
  1. Share the file + its merkle_proof path + merkle_root
  2. Any verifier recomputes: hash(leaf + proof_path) == root
  3. Sibling hashes are opaque — other files are not revealed
end note

Source -> FE  : Request proof path for one file
FE -> Cert    : GET /api/submissions/{id}/files/{file_hash}/proof
Cert -> DB    : Fetch proof path for file_hash
DB --> Cert   : { proof_path: [...sibling hashes...] }
Cert --> FE   : { file_hash, proof_path, merkle_root }
FE --> Source : Proof path to share with published document

== 8. Independent Verification (Public) ==

note over Source, Cert
  Any third party can independently verify authenticity
  without trusting this system:
  • RFC 3161 .tsr token verifiable with TSA public cert
  • OpenTimestamps .ots file verifiable against Bitcoin blockchain
end note

Source -> FE  : Provide certificate_id + merkle_root
FE -> Cert    : POST /api/verify\n{ certificate_id, merkle_root }
Cert -> TSA   : Verify .tsr token signature
Cert -> OTS   : Verify .ots file against blockchain
TSA --> Cert  : Valid / Invalid
OTS --> Cert  : Valid / Invalid
Cert --> FE   : Verification result\n{ rfc3161: valid, opentimestamps: valid }
FE --> Source : Timestamp proofs confirmed ✓

@enduml
